        "original_id": "7582baca-3ea2-5bca-a33a-e912800b0bdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Hampshire and Hampden Canal, Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway\n- Places: New Haven, Connecticut River, Northampton, Massachusetts, Tennessee River, Black Warrior-Tombigbee River system, Demopolis, Alabama\n\nFacts:\n- The Hampshire and Hampden Canal was the Massachusetts segment of an 86-mile canal.\n- The Hampshire and Hampden Canal once connected New Haven, Connecticut, to the Connecticut River north of Northampton, Massachusetts.\n- The Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway, also known as the Tenn-Tom, is a 234-mile man-made waterway.\n- The Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway extends from the Tennessee River to the junction of the Black Warrior-Tombigbee River system near Demopolis, Alabama, in the United States.",
